second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"2nd Duke of Newcastle, what year was he born?\", \"slot_hint\": \"birth_date\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 273, \"text\": \"Henry Cavendish, 2nd Duke of Newcastle Henry Cavendish, 2nd Duke of Newcastle-upon-Tyne, KG, PC (24 June 1630 – 26 July 1691), styled Viscount Mansfield until 1676, was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1660 to 1676, and then inherited the dukedom.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d00\", \"start\": 274, \"end\": 382, \"text\": \"Cavendish was the only son of William Cavendish, 1st Duke of Newcastle and his first wife, Elizabeth Basset.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d00\", \"start\": 383, \"end\": 474, \"text\": \"His maternal grandparents were William Basset and Judith Austen, daughter of Thomas Austen.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d00\", \"start\": 475, \"end\": 587, \"text\": \"In April 1660, Lord Mansfield was elected Member of Parliament (MP) for Derbyshire in the Convention Parliament.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d00\", \"start\": 588, \"end\": 624, \"text\": \"He was elected MP for Northumberland\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 212, \"text\": \"Henry Pelham-Clinton, 2nd Duke of Newcastle Henry Fiennes Pelham-Clinton, 2nd Duke of Newcastle-under-Lyne, KG, PC (16 April 1720 – 22 February 1794) was born in London, the second son of the 7th Earl of Lincoln.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d01\", \"start\": 213, \"end\": 335, \"text\": \"Henry's father died in 1728, and his brother, the 8th Earl of Lincoln, died in 1730, making Henry the 9th Earl of Lincoln.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d01\", \"start\": 336, \"end\": 425, \"text\": \"As he was still a minor, his guardian was his uncle, the 1st Duke of Newcastle-upon-Tyne.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d01\", \"start\": 426, \"end\": 494, \"text\": \"Newcastle was childless, and soon regarded Lord Lincoln as his heir.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d01\", \"start\": 495, \"end\": 582, \"text\": \"Newcastle, and his brother Henry Pelham, were the two most powerful men in England, and\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henry Cavendish, 2nd Duke of Newcastle\", \"scope\": \"Birth year\", \"claim\": \"Henry Cavendish, 2nd Duke of Newcastle was born on 24 June 1630.\", \"answer\": \"1630\", \"quote\": \"Henry Cavendish, 2nd Duke of Newcastle Henry Cavendish, 2nd Duke of Newcastle-upon-Tyne, KG, PC (24 June 1630 – 26 July 1691), styled Viscount Mansfield until 1676, was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1660 to 1676, and then inherited the dukedom.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0260-8ddeae739596:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henry Fiennes Pelham-Clinton, 2nd Duke of Newcastle-under-Lyne\", \"scope\": \"birth year\", \"claim\": \"Henry Fiennes Pelham-Clinton, 2nd Duke of Newcastle-under-Lyne was born on 16 April 1720.\", \"answer\": \"1720\", \"quote\": \"Henry Pelham-Clinton, 2nd Duke of Newcastle Henry Fiennes Pelham-Clinton, 2nd Duke of Newcastle-under-Lyne, KG, PC (16 April 1720 – 22 February 1794) was born in London, the second son of the 7th Earl of Lincoln.\"